{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1490178137,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMTYwMTM3ODI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1410","origin":"github"},"title":"Protect tests against connection issues","message":"As PR #1377 showed, we are (probably often) assuming that any connection will remain available during the tests if they were in the beginning. In that case it has been about a `AnnexRepo.drop()` in the test for `AnnexRepo.get()`. When using the testrepo from github (`clone` succeeded) `drop` failed, saying that github was \"unsafe\" and therefore it wouldn't count for the minimum number of required copies.\n\nI'm pretty sure this means, that `annex drop` wasn't able to connect to github at that point. So, the failing of `annex drop` is actually correct, but the test failed.","files":null}]}